                            {
                                "example_id": "641a0e1e-1882-48d7-9f68-9f681db06982",
                                "sense_id": "4f8fb62b-84fe-3ed5-8bf6-07bba253536b",
                                "text": "Coctive…Made by baking or exposing to heat, as a brick; coctile."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b40a6812-e9e6-3e70-a13e-16f773931395",
                        "entry_id": "e2263d9f-bb45-3027-ad2e-2a1147d60db9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Made by baking, or exposure to heat.",
                            "of earthenware"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d642ea6-4ef6-462c-9ff9-62169abec449",
                                "sense_id": "b40a6812-e9e6-3e70-a13e-16f773931395",
                                "text": "Theſe Corals…are made of a ſort of pale red Coctile Earth or Stone."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d4cf46e-c2af-4e74-a6c4-e35ade95578b",
                                "sense_id": "b40a6812-e9e6-3e70-a13e-16f773931395",
                                "text": "The excavations continued, and soon a most singularly shaped coctile vessel, or terra cotta urn…was brought to light."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb46d2eb-d517-4e7f-a70f-a640a19d5671",
                                "sense_id": "b40a6812-e9e6-3e70-a13e-16f773931395",
                                "text": "Now, these tiles are of the coctile kind, or which have been baked red like bricks or common red “roofing tiles.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4bca309-d6d3-4012-8557-7c42af0623a4",
                                "sense_id": "b40a6812-e9e6-3e70-a13e-16f773931395",
                                "text": "An oval platform of stone…stands out inside a perimeter frame of beige coctile brick with a fishbone formation."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dc7d2c62-c2c6-3af1-ab9e-0d0174cb3a12",
                        "entry_id": "e2263d9f-bb45-3027-ad2e-2a1147d60db9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Made by baking, or exposure to heat.",
                            "of bread"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b233315f-ce64-4fb1-9538-bedb2a867ebb",
                                "sense_id": "dc7d2c62-c2c6-3af1-ab9e-0d0174cb3a12",
                                "text": "Was ever coctile product more appetizing to hungry mortals! The good Dr. Talmage…acknowledges a heavy debt to good bread as a stimulant to an overdrained brain."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6e51f584-4927-370c-b584-63db8d724234",
                        "entry_id": "e2263d9f-bb45-3027-ad2e-2a1147d60db9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Built of baked bricks."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0de0554-6faa-41a7-9a60-ab683c2543fc",
                                "sense_id": "6e51f584-4927-370c-b584-63db8d724234",
                                "text": "From the tiles and skylights of a coctile edifice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69edc7ff-b3d0-44ca-89cb-63d8cd45afbb",
                                "sense_id": "6e51f584-4927-370c-b584-63db8d724234",
                                "text": "Beyond this region spread dead levels, which…resembled the sea. From the city’s lofty walls stretched on all sides…flatness and luxuriance. What, then, could taste divine and power accomplish…to transport thither a primeval forest, and to pile up coctile mountains to place it on. Such was the design of the Hanging Gardens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f8fec54-9e6e-49ae-a6e6-5a31fdea237c",
                                "sense_id": "6e51f584-4927-370c-b584-63db8d724234",
                                "text": "The “coctile” texture of the wall is visible where there are lacks of plaster and elements of stone appear too."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
